{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788185927,"nonce":"zkz5ZMNmJRKyTKvNdGZDIteHb5E=","title":"seek-at-will verb: autonomous combat via SeekAndKill, so a raid is not per-pawn micromanagement","message":"Raised by Evan, 2026-08-31: \"I hope combat uses our seekandkill mod, there would\nbe too much micromanagement otherwise.\" He is right, and the verb does not exist.\n\nWHAT IS ALREADY SHIPPED (3.4, closed today)\n\n`draft`, `undraft`, `attack`, `equip`, `wear`, `drop`, `fire-at-will`,\n`man-turret`, `rescue`, `capture`, `arrest`. So the agent CAN arm a colonist and\norder it to shoot a specific target. That is the micromanagement path: draft\neach pawn, issue an attack order, watch, re-order. Over a ten-day run with\nraids, that is the whole play loop spent on combat.\n\nWHAT IS MISSING\n\n`SeekAndKill` (Dorian.SeekAndKill) is loaded on the agent bench and is exactly\nthe answer: a per-pawn \"Seek at Will\" toggle that hands combat to an autonomous\nsquad brain — threat clustering, priority dispatch, cover-aware formations,\nmelee front / snipers rear, self-defense reflex. Toggle a pawn on and it fights\nraids by itself. **Nothing in AutoRimmer's ~80 verbs can set that toggle.**\n\nVERIFIED AGAINST THE MOD'S OWN SOURCE (not assumed)\n\n- **Perspective Shift is NOT on the bench**, so PS's gizmo is absent and\n  SeekAndKill supplies its own. The toggle set is\n  `SeekAndKillGameComponent.OwnSeekSet` (`HashSet\u003cint\u003e` of pawn ids), scribed as\n  `SK_SeekPawns` — and scribed ONLY when PS is absent, which is our case.\n- **The widget gate to reproduce**, `Patch_PawnGetGizmos.ShowsSeekGizmo`:\n  `pawn.Faction == Faction.OfPlayer \u0026\u0026 !pawn.RaceProps.Animal \u0026\u0026 !pawn.Drafted\n  \u0026\u0026 !pawn.WorkTagIsDisabled(WorkTags.Violent)`.\n  Note `!Drafted` — Seek at Will is for UNDRAFTED pawns. That is the whole\n  point: it is autonomous combat, the opposite of drafting.\n- **The API**: `SeekRegistry.IsToggled / Toggle / StanceOf / SetStance /\n  ShouldSeek / AnySeekPawns`.\n- **Toggle through `MpCompat.SyncedToggleSeek(pawn)`, not `SeekRegistry.Toggle`\n  directly.** The gizmo's own comment says why: the seek set is saved state the\n  think tree reads on every client.\n- **There is a stance**: `SeekStance` Close/Medium/Far, a right-click\n  fire-distance menu, persisted as `SK_StanceByPawn`. Medium is never stored.\n  Expose it — \"hold back\" vs \"close in\" is a real tactical lever.\n\nTHE DESIGN QUESTION THIS OPENS, and it is bigger than one verb\n\nEvery AutoRimmer verb so far is vanilla-only. This one targets a THIRD-PARTY\nmod, and AutoRimmer must not take a hard reference on it — SeekAndKill is not a\ndependency, it merely happens to be on the bench. So:\n\n- Reach it by reflection, and answer cleanly when the mod is absent rather than\n  throwing. SeekAndKill's own `PSInterop` is the template: it reflects into\n  Perspective Shift, and if PS is present but cannot be neutralized it stays\n  inactive for the session rather than running two brains.\n- Decide and RECORD in DESIGN's decisions log what a mod-aware verb looks like\n  in general: how it is named, how it reports \"mod not loaded\", and whether it\n  lives beside the vanilla verbs or in a namespace of its own. This is not a\n  one-off — the entire point of the platform is testing mods (5.1/5.2 target\n  Factions and Guests), so a documented pattern pays for itself immediately.\n\nWHY THIS IS M1-CRITICAL, alongside 3.5\n\n4.3 is \"survive 10 days\". Raids are the thing that kills a colony, and without\nthis verb every raid is a manual draft-and-order sequence for every colonist.\nThat is not \"an agent playing RimWorld\", it is an agent playing a tactics puzzle\nby hand, and it will dominate the play loop (4.2) and the checklist budget (4.4).\nWith it, combat readiness is a one-time toggle per pawn plus a stance.\n\nAcceptance\n\n- `seek-at-will {pawns:[…], on:true|false, stance?:\"close\"|\"medium\"|\"far\"}` —\n  plural, batch-first like every other action verb.\n- The gate is `ShowsSeekGizmo`, clause for clause, cited by file and member; a\n  drafted pawn, an animal, a non-player pawn and a Violent-disabled pawn are\n  each REFUSED with a named gate rather than silently skipped.\n- Toggling goes through `MpCompat.SyncedToggleSeek`.\n- The result echoes durable state read BACK: is the pawn in the seek set now,\n  and what stance. Not a hope.\n- When SeekAndKill is not loaded the verb answers with a clear \"mod not present\"\n  rather than an exception, and `status`/`digest` can say whether it is there.\n- The `pawn` observer reports seek state and stance, so the agent can verify\n  without re-issuing the toggle.\n- Demonstrated live: toggle two armed colonists on, spawn a hostile raid with\n  `dev:incident`, advance, and show the pawns engaged and the raid resolved with\n  NO draft and NO attack order issued — the journal is the proof, it should\n  contain the one `action` row for the toggle and nothing else per pawn.","files":null}]}